Task 4:
///Lab: Authentication bypass via information disclosure///

Open the page in burp and log in as wiener/peter. Send the GET /my-account?id=wiener request to repeater. Change it to /admin.
In the response you can see you can access only if you are localhost. To simulate this change the method to TRACE and send the request:
HTTP/2 200 OK
Content-Type: message/http
X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
Content-Length: 667

TRACE /admin HTTP/1.1
Host: 0aae0053047d353e81fdb66300490026.web-security-academy.net
user-agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:149.0 Gecko/20100101 Firefox/149.0
...
...
te: trailers
x-custom-ip-authorization: 188.36.20.172
cookie: session=zOX2KlbKXzKCQE8GSvkvGdGquL8oWsBV
Content-Length: 0

So the X-custom-ip-authorization is the header which we have to simulate. To do this go to proxy/Match and replace. Add a new HTTP match leave everything unchaged, change only the replace field to this:
X-Custom-IP-Authorization: 127.0.0.1
Click to ok, and refresh your browser. Now you have admin panel...delete carlos and the lab is solved.

Task 5:
///Lab: Information disclosure in version control history///

Open the site in burp. Paste the /.git to the end of the URL, and you will see the repository of the site. get the whole repo with
wget -r https://0a8300660447a0cb81434dbe00eb00f3.web-security-academy.net/.git/
If you open 1 by 1 the files in the file called "COMMIT_EDITMSG" you will find this:
'Remove admin password from config'
This means that the admin password was in a config file. But the site saves the actions in a log file, so go into the log directory, and there will be a file called HEAD. If you open it you will find this:
